WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.820
Put an electrode inside a resting frog muscle fibre, at the endplate, where the

2
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.440
nerve ends. Stimulate nothing.

3
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:15.820
Small depolarizations still arrive at random times.

4
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:21.180
Each is about the same size, and each is far too small to fire the fibre.

5
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.100
What are they?

6
00:00:23.483 --> 00:00:27.123
These are miniature endplate potentials.

7
00:00:27.543 --> 00:00:32.703
Fatt and Katz attributed them to spontaneous release of acetylcholine from the nerve

8
00:00:32.703 --> 00:00:39.203
terminal. Del Castillo and Katz asked whether a nerve impulse evokes the same units.

9
00:00:40.323 --> 00:00:45.963
They bathed the frog junction in less calcium and more magnesium, which cut release

10
00:00:45.963 --> 00:00:51.803
to a trickle. Now an impulse often produced nothing at all, a failure.

11
00:00:52.717 --> 00:00:56.697
When a response did come, its size was not random.

12
00:00:57.517 --> 00:01:03.657
The amplitudes clustered at the size of one miniature, at twice that, and at three

13
00:01:03.657 --> 00:01:07.917
times that. So the evoked response came in packets.

14
00:01:08.897 --> 00:01:14.537
Each packet is a quantum, a packet of many molecules, later identified with the

15
00:01:14.537 --> 00:01:16.137
contents of one vesicle.

16
00:01:16.697 --> 00:01:19.277
It is not one molecule of acetylcholine.

17
00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:26.090
The mean quantal content is the average number of quanta one impulse releases.

18
00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:31.130
Take a made-up frog junction in low calcium and high magnesium.

19
00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:38.390
The mean miniature and the mean response, failures included, are both 0.40

20
00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:42.650
millivolts. So the ratio is one quantum per stimulus.

21
00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:49.930
Failures give a second estimate, since 74 of 200 stimuli gave no response.

22
00:01:50.783 --> 00:01:57.363
Under a Poisson model, minus the natural log of 0.37 is 0.99.

23
00:01:58.163 --> 00:01:59.443
The two estimates agree.

24
00:02:00.343 --> 00:02:06.983
Now restore normal calcium, and suppose 60 quanta of 0.40 millivolts each.

25
00:02:07.703 --> 00:02:13.523
If they add linearly, the response is 24 millivolts, and as an illustration, the

26
00:02:13.523 --> 00:02:14.923
fibre fires at 12.

27
00:02:14.923 --> 00:02:18.863
The safety factor, the ratio of the two, is 2.

28
00:02:19.717 --> 00:02:26.457
In myasthenia gravis, fewer receptors mean a smaller quantal size, and 60 of them

29
00:02:26.457 --> 00:02:27.637
still fire the fibre.

30
00:02:28.357 --> 00:02:33.137
But suppose release runs down by 25 percent to 45 quanta.

31
00:02:33.777 --> 00:02:37.897
The response is then 10.8 millivolts, and the fibre fails.

32
00:02:38.997 --> 00:02:43.937
Miniature size also depends on vesicle filling, so confirm with a receptor count.

33
00:02:43.937 --> 00:02:50.277
Even so, smaller packets point after the synapse, and fewer packets point before it.
